WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.571
<v Nina Kowalski>Hi, this is Nina from Ferro & Vance. Our card on file just expired and we also moved offices, so I need to update both billing details.</v>

00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:24.700
<v Morgan Lee>Happy to help with that. Since this is a billing change, I need to verify your identity first — can you confirm the name and email on the account?</v>

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.686
<v Nina Kowalski>Nina Kowalski, nina.kowalski@ferrovance.example.</v>

00:00:27.386 --> 00:00:37.243
<v Morgan Lee>Thanks. And for verification, can you give me the last four digits of the card currently on file, and your date of birth?</v>

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:43.514
<v Nina Kowalski>Last four are 8823, and my date of birth is April 3, 1985.</v>

00:00:44.214 --> 00:01:02.214
<v Morgan Lee>That matches what's on file, you're verified. For the new card, I'll send you a secure link to our billing portal rather than take the number directly — same as when you signed up. What's the best email to send that to?</v>

00:01:02.914 --> 00:01:04.200
<v Nina Kowalski>Same email, nina.kowalski@ferrovance.example.</v>

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:13.043
<v Morgan Lee>Sent. While you're doing that, let's update your billing address for the office move — what's the new address?</v>

00:01:13.743 --> 00:01:17.600
<v Nina Kowalski>It's 1420 Sutro Terrace, Suite 4, Reno, NV, 89502.</v>

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:26.014
<v Morgan Lee>Got it, updating that now... billing address is updated. Have you completed the card update on your end?</v>

00:01:26.714 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Nina Kowalski>Just finished, it shows the new card ending in 2290.</v>

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:38.986
<v Morgan Lee>Confirmed on our end too, ending in 2290, active starting with next month's billing cycle. Anything else?</v>

00:01:39.686 --> 00:01:43.543
<v Nina Kowalski>No, that covers it, thanks for the quick help.</v>

00:01:44.243 --> 00:01:48.100
<v Morgan Lee>Of course, have a good rest of your day.</v>
